From b0ae1c8d2cd85582e2e72bcb2054a409689fd981 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luis Chamberlain <mcgrof@do-not-panic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 15:51:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add a rendered replay of recorded action traces (--rl-replay)

Play a trace recorded from the headless bridge through the normal
rendered game so a learned policy can be watched. "etr --rl-replay
TRACE [LOG]" reads a header (course, group, seed, dt, wind, light,
mirror, autoquit) and one action per physics tick, skips the menus by
selecting the traced course for the first player, and advances every
state by exactly dt instead of the measured frame time so the physics
is the same computation the headless run performed. The racing loop
takes its steering flip-flops from the trace and logs position,
velocity, items and collisions per tick to LOG, which a client can
diff against the headless trajectory of the same trace. With
autoquit=1 the game exits a few seconds after the finish.

Signed-off-by: Luis Chamberlain <mcgrof@do-not-panic.com>
